      "task": "Verify all six supplied equalities by converting each claimed logarithm value into a power relation; merely selecting the already supplied logarithm values would not perform the task.",
      "derivation": "a: 3^2=9. b: 5^3=125. c: 10^(-1)=1/10. d: 4^(1/2)=sqrt(4)=2. e: 2^(-6)=1/(2^6)=1/64. f: (1/3)^(-4)=3^4=81. All bases are positive and unequal to 1; all arguments are positive. Each supplied equality is therefore valid.",
      "complete_result": "All six are true, independently verified by the six displayed power identities.",
      "distinction": "Logarithm as exponent, including negative and fractional exponents and a reciprocal base."
    },
    {
      "number": "726",
      "task": "Express all six given power exponents in logarithmic notation, preserving the roles of base and result.",
      "derivation": "2^5=32 gives log_2 32=5; 3^(-3)=1/27 gives log_3(1/27)=-3; 12^1=12 gives log_12 12=1; 20^0=1 gives log_20 1=0; 25^(1/2)=5 gives log_25 5=1/2; 8^(-1/3)=1/2 gives log_8(1/2)=-1/3.",
      "complete_result": ["log_2 32=5","log_3(1/27)=-3","log_12 12=1","log_20 1=0","log_25 5=1/2","log_8(1/2)=-1/3"],
      "distinction": "Inverse conversion from power notation to logarithm notation, not arithmetic substitution."
    },
    {
      "number": "727",
