      "derivation": "f is y=2x+3 with x>=0. It is a closed-endpoint ray from (0,3), through (1,5) and (2,7), continuing indefinitely up and right; domain [0,+infinity), range [3,+infinity). Swapping input and output gives x=2y+3 with y>=0, equivalently g: y=(x-3)/2 with x>=3. Thus D_g=[3,+infinity) and R_g=[0,+infinity). Its graph is the closed-endpoint ray from (3,0), through (5,1) and (7,2), indefinitely up and right. Corresponding ordered pairs exchange coordinates; the rays are mirror images across y=x. A finite drawn window is not a finite domain.",
